<title>ISRAEL: Bank of Israel cuts rate 0.3 points to 13.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Israel cuts rate 0.3 points to 13.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>JERUSALEM 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Israel said on Monday it was lowering its key lending rate for March by 0.3 percentage point to an annualised 13.9 percent.</p>
<p>The rate is the one charged commercial banks at daily and weekly monetary tenders.</p>
<p>The bank said its decision to lower rate was taken against a continuing fall in inflation and a slowing economy. The bank said the slower economy enabled the bank to continue easing rates although there were factors demanding continued monetary restraint.</p>
</text>
